Red Hood turned off the trail and when she spotted a branchy spruce, headed right to it. She made herself comfortable under the thick crown, ate a pasty with cabbage and then leaned against a wide trunk. Red Hood enjoyed quiet and coolness of her shelter and didn't notice how she fell into a doze. She never had such a wonderful sleep.
She woke up at night because her entire body became numb. Being half-awake girl could not immediately orientate herself, where she was and what was going on, but little by little reconstructed in memory last events and it became clear that she lied under the tree till darkness. She looked around trying to find the trail, when suddenly felt her heart missed a beat. In thickening shadows one could hardly discern anything. The girl had no idea where to go.